  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent 7-day mean reversion is observed (true outcome < model forecast by > 3σ).",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0.33) to avoid premature spikes.",
    "Cap forecast above 10% above recent 30-day high if sentiment is bullish (sentiment > 0.50) to prevent overshoot.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if model forecast is > 1.5σ above 30-day moving average, reduce by 15-20%.",
    "If sentiment is volatile (fluctuating ±0.33), use weighted average of 30d history and 7d sentiment to smooth forecasts."
  ]
}
